  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "DPU steps down again in FY27 (to ~11.9c declared, ~11.1c owner flow after unit-paid fees and maintenance capex) on NA non-renewals and swap repricing, troughs in FY28 through the divestment programme, then grows 1.5-2% a year. Capitalised at a 7.5% SGD cost of equity.",
    "bull": "FY27 is the trough: NA space re-lets to cloud/colo, recycling into Japan/APAC DCs is accretive, and DPU compounds ~3% from FY28. 7.0% cost of equity.",
    "bear": "North American enterprise data centres keep emptying, re-letting needs capex, FX and divestment dilution compound: DPU falls ~4% a year for two years and then grows ~1%. 8.0% cost of equity."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Value the per-unit distributable flow an owner actually receives, net of the management fees settled in new units and of the maintenance capex distributable income ignores, capitalised at the SGD cost of equity with no debt deduction (the flow is post-interest and post-perpetuals). NAV is a cross-check only: IAS 40 values are appraiser cap rates, and the stock trades at ~1.10x NAV.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "North American data centres (46.5% of AUM) carry enterprise-tenant non-renewal risk outside primary markets; re-letting speed and fit-out capex drive the bear/base gap",
      "~S$600m of interest-rate hedges reprice in FY26/27 and leverage rises to ~37.5%; every 100bp on unhedged debt is ~S$3-7m of DI",
      "USD and JPY translation: ~92.5% of distributable income is SGD-hedged near term, but not structurally",
      "Capital recycling: S$500-600m of NA divestments must be redeployed at a positive spread or DPU steps down further",
      "Cost of equity: a 50bp move in the SGD rate moves the base value by roughly 8-10%"
    ]
  },
